			(property "Description" "Track Signaled in Both Directions:  Governs bi-directional signal territory (often controlled by  Centralized Traffic Control, or CTC).  Under Rule 261, block signal  indications supersede train superiority for both opposing and following movements on the same track, allowing the dispatcher to dynamically change the direction of traffic by clearing signals."
